<<~ ahu slot=`#/0-house-ground`>>

!! 0. House ground (READ)
* otakiage.mem (revised 2026-09-12): the five-stage lifecycle rides tags `lifecycle/designed|standing|folded|harvest|retiring`, kind rides `kind/rite`. A carrier with no lifecycle tag stands UNGOVERNED. `lares meme sitting` names burn candidates (folded/retiring with nothing inbound, plus standing harvest rooms) and burns nothing; a burn happens in front of someone ("do not leave it silently"). Its own field survey already cites Ahrens' fleeting/permanent ladder, Matuschak evergreen, Appleton seedling/budding/evergreen, Gwern status+confidence. The memory-stage reuses that ladder; it does not need a new one.
* Memory index (READ): the mempalace/sensorium is BURNED (2026-10-13) and the re-stand is DEFERRED until the founded-Lararium proof (2026-10-27). project_next_arc_sensorium_sidecar.md and project_sensorium_li_ki_canon.md (dated July/Sept) describe an arc the index marks deferred or burned; do not build on them as live. reference_mempalace_repair.md describes a Chroma sidecar that the index says no longer stands. The mempalace/ directory exists in the checkout (README READ: local-first, verbatim storage, 96.6% R@5 on LongMemEval, "does not summarize"); it is a vendored submodule, not house canon.
* grep bags/ finds talk-story/hoike/moolelo in offering.mem, realm-bag-brief.mem, k15-wave-b-lane.mem, test-recut-road.mem and others (names only; bodies not read). Talk-story and hoike skills exist (listed in the skill roster) and already close in moolelo / hoike / suspension.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/1-neuroscience-of-memory-staging-with-operationa`>>

!! 1. Neuroscience of memory staging, with operational analogues
All [RECALL] unless marked; primary sources the controller can verify.
# Working memory + global workspace (Baddeley & Hitch 1974; Baars 1988; Dehaene's global neuronal workspace). Small capacity, broadcast to many specialists. Analogue: the plan/owed stage is the workspace: small, one line per act, broadcast to every lane. Cap its size; overflow forces promotion or burn.
# Hippocampal indexing (Teyler & DiScenna 1986). The hippocampus stores pointers to cortical patterns, not the content. Analogue: the stage holds an index tiddler whose fields point (loulou/transclusion) at the scout report, the commit, the carrier. Index cheap, content elsewhere.
# Complementary learning systems (McClelland, McNaughton, O'Reilly 1995; Kumaran, Hassabis, McClelland 2016 update). Fast episodic learning protects slow semantic structure from catastrophic interference. Analogue: fast writes land on the daemon wiki's working stage; canon `.mem` changes slowly under ruling. Never write episodes straight into canon.
# Systems consolidation + sleep replay (Squire; Buzsaki sharp-wave ripples; Diekelmann & Born 2010). Offline replay moves episodes to cortex. Analogue: a scheduled "sitting" between waves (the existing `meme sitting` shape) replays the stage rows and proposes promotions. Replay is offline, off the critical path.
# Reconsolidation (Nader, Schafe, LeDoux 2000). A recalled memory becomes labile and rewritable. Analogue: reading a stage row at boot is the moment to re-verify and re-write it. Rule: a row read at cold boot carries a `last-tended` stamp updated only when re-checked against the repo; an unchecked row is shown as unchecked. This is the cure for the house's stale-memory problem ("memories age; check what they name").
# Schema-dependent consolidation (Tse et al. 2007; van Kesteren et al. 2012). Info fitting an existing schema consolidates fast; schema-violating info needs slower handling. Analogue: a row that fits an existing carrier slot promotes quickly via fold; a row contradicting held canon routes to hoike (talk-story floor), not silent merge. This matches the "divergence surfaces" law.
# Forgetting as a feature (Anderson; Richards & Frankland 2017, "The persistence and transience of memory"). Transience aids generalization and flexibility. Analogue: otakiage. Burn finished rows with thanks; forgetting is a ruled rite, not neglect.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/2-ai-agent-memory-developments`>>

!! 2. AI agent memory developments
* MemGPT / Letta [RECALL; Packer et al. 2023, arXiv 2310.08560]: OS-style tiers: in-context core memory blocks, recall (message history), archival (vector). The agent edits its own blocks via tools. Failure: the agent overwrites or bloats its blocks; context pressure triggers lossy summarization.
* Letta sleep-time compute [SEARCH: arXiv 2504.13171, "Sleep-time Compute: Beyond Inference Scaling at Test-time", Lin, Snell et al.; reports ~5x less test-time compute at equal accuracy on Stateful GSM-Symbolic/AIME; best when the query is predictable from context]. A background agent rewrites shared memory blocks between turns. Failure: consolidation agent confabulates or invalidates good records; unobserved writes. A separate May 2026 paper "Language Models Need Sleep" (arXiv 2605.26099) is a different work (fast-weight layers) [SEARCH]; do not conflate.
* Generative Agents [RECALL; Park et al. 2023, arXiv 2304.03442]: append-only memory stream; retrieval scored by recency + importance (LLM-rated 1-10) + relevance; periodic reflection when summed importance crosses a threshold writes higher-level notes citing sources. Failure: reflection compounds an early error; importance scores uncalibrated. (CORRECTED in section 5: recency decays over simulated game hours, not wall time; still a clock, so the house substitutes act-count.)
* A-MEM [SEARCH: arXiv 2502.12110, Zettelkasten-style linked atomic notes, new memories can update old ones; multi-hop gains on LoCoMo reported by the authors; several paper versions exist, cite the version]. Failure: automatic link and rewrite of old notes can drift history; needs the original kept.
* Mem0 / Mem0g (Chhikara et al. 2025) and Zep / Graphiti (Rasmussen et al. 2025) [SEARCH: only a 2026 survey, arXiv 2604.01707, was seen, classing Mem0 as flat vector with a graph variant and Zep as hierarchical temporal graph; primary papers not opened]. Zep's bi-temporal edges (event time vs ingestion time) fit the house idea of valid-as-of-sync. Both are web2 SaaS or service-shaped by default; barred from the stack proper (see section 3 law check); take the ideas only.
* Anthropic [SEARCH: platform.claude.com memory-tool docs page, anthropic.com/news/context-management; not opened]. The memory tool is client-side: Claude reads and writes files in a /memories directory the developer's own code executes; context editing clears stale tool results. Anthropic's own reported figures: +39% (memory + context editing) and +29% (context editing alone) on an internal agentic-search eval, testimony from the vendor. Relevance: this is the same file-directory pattern the house uses with flat .md memory; the wiki can BE that directory's backing store.
* Reflexion [RECALL; Shinn et al. 2023, arXiv 2303.11366]: after a failed attempt the agent writes a verbal self-critique into an episodic buffer and reads it next try. Failure: a wrong self-diagnosis persists and misleads later runs; no external check. Related: Voyager skill library [RECALL; Wang et al. 2023], procedural memory as verified code.
* Cross-cutting failure modes seen across these: stale state read as current; confabulated "memories" from summarizer; self-written feedback never verified; unbounded growth; retrieval returning plausible but superseded rows. Benchmarks like LongMemEval and LoCoMo measure retrieval, rarely staleness [RECALL].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/3-design-the-memory-stage-on-the-daemon-wiki`>>

!! 3. Design: the memory-stage on the daemon wiki
Principle: a stage is a set of TAGS plus an index view on the existing daemon wiki, not a new store, not a new plane. Reuse the lifecycle ladder; extend it downward with one pre-stage.

Tiers (proposal; names are the operator's to rule):
| Tier | Content now | Home | Tag family |h
| Working | plan.md, owed.md, resume sheets | daemon wiki working stage (wikis/&lt;slug>/working, wikis-first writes) | `stage/working` + `lifecycle/designed`-equivalent row tag `row/open` |
| Episodic | scout reports, walks, handbacks, incident notes | same wiki, one tiddler per event, append-only | `stage/episodic`, `kind/scout|walk|incident` |
| Semantic | canon `.mem` carriers | bags/ (git-tracked, canon) | existing `lifecycle/*` |
| Procedural | lead law, briefs, working-procedures | bags/ `.mem` | `kind/rite|brief`, lifecycle/standing |
| Feedback | what the flat feedback_*.md files hold | wiki working stage, promoted to procedural by ruling | `stage/feedback`, `recurs/N` |

Consolidation rite (maps onto existing machinery): a working row earns promotion by (a) a witness (commit sha, test, measurement), the same witness law `standing` already requires, and (b) a sitting. Conflict with held canon opens a talk-story floor; the floor closes in moolelo (promote), hoike (kept dissent), or suspension. Promotion = pour a carrier in bags/ via PR, and the working row becomes a pointer (`lifecycle/folded` shape: "folded to lar:&#47;&#47;/..."). Fast to canon: never. The stage proposes; the operator's ruling promotes.

Cold-boot retrieval: the controller reads, in order: (1) the stage index view (open rows only, each with last-tended causal stamp and unchecked flag); (2) the pono roadmap carrier; (3) the controller handoff. Episodic detail loads by pointer only on need. Target a fixed small boot set, so boot cost does not grow with history.

Forgetting: `meme sitting` extended to stage rows: closed rows with a landed witness are candidates; the burn happens at the land (existing "o-takiage at every land" feedback), announced in the commit line, never silent. Episodic tiddlers age out into a harvest room when nothing points at them.

Self-improvement loop: incident tiddler (what happened, the tell from #/off-true) -> recurrence counter (`recurs/N`, counted by repeat incidents, no clock) -> at N=2 a sitting proposes a procedural change (a feedback rule or a guard test, red-first per house law) -> operator rules -> promoted. Reflexion's lesson: a self-written lesson stays `unverified` until a later incident shows it held; flag lessons that never fired as burn candidates. Generative Agents' reflection maps to the sitting, with importance = recurrence count and blast radius, not an LLM score.

History: git holds canon history (bags/); the disk projection mirrors wikis/ working state; Automerge holds the live causal log. A working row's edits live in the CRDT log between projections. MEASURED (controller + scout): `git ls-files wikis` returns 0; .gitignore line 57 says named wikis are checked in, line 58 ignores wikis/scratch/. See section 5.

House-law check:
* Web3/local-first: no Mem0/Zep/Letta Cloud. Take patterns (tiers, bi-temporal stamps, sleep-time sitting), run them on the daemon wiki. A local embedding index is optional and, per the burned mempalace, a deferred arc.
* No global now: replace recency with causal stamps ("rows since", wave number, commit sha). No wall-clock decay.
* Wikis-first writes: the stage lives where AI writes already land; only a sitting plus ruling crosses into bags/.
* Operator originates: the stage proposes, never promotes; divergence from canon surfaces to hoike.
* Idempotent single-operator refound: stage tiddlers need deterministic ids (derived from the event/row key) so a re-pour reproduces the same tiddlers. Open question; mechanism unmeasured.

<<~/ahu>>

