<<~ ahu slot=`#/5-round-2-primary-pages-repo-measure-talked-out`>>

!! 5. Round 2: primary pages, repo measure, talked-out questions

!!! 5a. Primary reads [FETCHED = page opened this session via WebFetch, which summarizes the page with a small model; read as abstract-level]
* Sleep-time compute, arXiv 2504.13171 [FETCHED abstract]: model reasons offline about a context before any query, "pre-computing useful quantities". ~5x less test-time compute at equal accuracy; accuracy up to +13% (Stateful GSM-Symbolic) and +18% (Stateful AIME) with more sleep-time compute; 2.5x lower average cost per query when queries share a context (Multi-Query GSM-Symbolic). Effect tracks query predictability. Evidence: two modified benchmarks plus one SWE case study. CORRECTION: my earlier "consolidation agent writes memory blocks" came from a tutorial site; the paper itself concerns precomputation over a context, not memory-block consolidation. Letta's product behavior stays [SEARCH] only.
* A-MEM, arXiv 2502.12110 [FETCHED abstract]: on each new memory the system builds a note with contextual description, keywords, tags; links it to historical memories by similarity; integration can UPDATE descriptions/attributes of existing memories ("memory evolution"). Reports gains over baselines across six foundation models; abstract gives no figures and no retrieval method. CORRECTION: "multi-hop gains on LoCoMo" was snippet-level; not seen on the abstract page. Failure mode (existing notes rewritten, history drifts) is my inference from the evolution step, [INFERENCE].
* Anthropic memory tool [FETCHED full docs page]: stable; client-side, Claude requests file ops under /memories (view, create, str_replace, insert, delete, rename), the application executes them against storage the developer controls; the API injects a protocol: "ALWAYS VIEW YOUR MEMORY DIRECTORY BEFORE DOING ANYTHING ELSE... ASSUME INTERRUPTION: Your context window might be reset at any moment". Docs advise: cap file sizes, expire memory not accessed in a long time, path-traversal checks, strip sensitive data. Documents a multisession pattern: an initializer session writes a progress log + feature checklist; each session opens by reading them and updates before ending; "Mark a feature complete only after end-to-end verification". Directly shaped like plan.md/owed.md and supports the stage index design; the docs' own expiry advice matches otakiage.
* Context editing [FETCHED page, first 100k of 107k chars]: beta header context-management-2025-06-27; `clear_tool_uses_20250919` clears oldest tool results past a trigger (default 100,000 input tokens, keeps 3 most recent), `clear_thinking_20251015`; client keeps full history; as context nears the threshold Claude is warned to save to memory files. The page recommends server-side compaction for most long conversations. Anthropic's +39%/+29% figures stay [SEARCH] (blog snippet), vendor testimony.
* Generative Agents, arXiv 2304.03442 [FETCHED abstract + ar5iv text, first 100k of 144k chars]: stream of natural-language observations. Retrieval score = recency + importance + relevance, each min-max scaled to [0,1], all weights 1. Recency: exponential decay 0.995 over SANDBOX GAME HOURS since last retrieval (a simulated clock, correcting my earlier "wall clock"). Importance: LLM rates 1-10 at creation ("poignant", mundane=1). Relevance: cosine similarity of embeddings. Reflection fires when summed importance of recent events exceeds 150, about 2-3 times per simulated day. Ablation: observation, planning, reflection each add believability. House move: keep the trigger shape (accumulated weight crosses a threshold), swap the clock for act-count and the LLM score for recurrence + blast radius.
* MemGPT, arXiv 2310.08560 [FETCHED abstract]: "virtual context management" borrowing OS hierarchical memory; moves information between fast and slow tiers; interrupts coordinate control flow; tested on document analysis and multi-session chat. Specifics of core/recall/archival tiers and self-edit tools remain [RECALL].
* CLS, Kumaran, Hassabis, McClelland 2016 [FETCHED abstract, PubMed 27315762]: neocortex = slow structured knowledge; hippocampus = fast individual experiences; replay can weight experience statistics by current goals and support generalization; neocortical learning can be FAST when new information fits existing structure (this confirms the schema point in 1.6 and corrects my "fast writes never to canon" absolutism: a fit-the-schema row may fold quickly).
* Hippocampal indexing, Teyler & Rudy 2007, Hippocampus 17(12):1158-69, doi 10.1002/hipo.20350 [SEARCH: bibliographic data + a gloss; abstract/full text not opened; my first PubMed guess returned an unrelated paper]. Gloss: neocortex holds content, hippocampus holds an index of the loci; a partial cue reactivating the index retrieves the episode. The review concludes the theory has aged well.
* Reconsolidation, Nader, Schafe, LeDoux 2000, Nature 406(6797):722-6, doi 10.1038/35021052 [SEARCH: PubMed record + abstract gloss; page not opened; my first PubMed guess was wrong]. Reactivated consolidated fear memories return to a labile state needing de novo protein synthesis to restabilize (rat amygdala, anisomycin). Caveat: a rodent fear-memory result; my "recall makes any memory editable" operational analogue is an analogy, not a finding.

!!! 5b. Repo measure folded into the design
`git ls-files wikis` returns 0 files; .gitignore:57 promises named wikis are checked in; :58 ignores wikis/scratch/. So today a wikis/ stage row reaches git only by (i) pouring a carrier in bags/, or (ii) a named wiki being checked in. LEAN: a two-leg stage. The working stage (plan/owed/feedback, high churn) lives in a named wiki that is NOT tracked by default: CRDT log plus disk projection hold it, and its loss is cheap by design. Anything that must outlive a refound reaches git only by promotion to a bags/ carrier (the existing rite), plus ONE thin tracked named wiki for the episodic tier (scout reports, incident rows) that cold sessions need after a clone. Reason: tracking the churning working stage would put every plan line into git and fight the tree-clean witness; promotion is the checkpoint; this also keeps "refound is idempotent" honest because only promoted, witnessed rows must reproduce. Unmeasured: what name/slug a checked-in stage wiki takes and whether wikis/lares-history (the .gitignore example) is the intended precedent.

!!! 5c. The four questions, talked out (two rounds each; all voices mine, so this is testimony, not a floor)
Gaia/Elyncia anchor: a household shrine keeps today's offering on the niche (working), the year's ofuda until the year-end rite (episodic), and the temple register (canon). A Lar binds to a PLACE; the niche is not the temple.
# Does `stage/*` extend `lifecycle/*` or sit beside it? R1: extend (one filter, one ladder). R2 against: a working row has no witness, and `meme check` enforces witnesses on governed stages, so putting an unwitnessed row in `lifecycle/designed` hands the gate a row it must read as open `-> ?`, and tag family collisions would mean every plan line enters the governed count (54 of 726 today). SETTLED: sibling family `stage/*` for unpoured rows; a row that is poured as a carrier takes `lifecycle/*` at the pour. The niche and the register stay different shelves.
# Where does the stage live (which wiki)? R1: the daemon wiki the operator named. R2: the operator said "daemon wiki", and the daemon wiki is the place the crew already addresses; a Lar binds to place. SETTLED in shape: the daemon's own named wiki hosts the stage. Slug and tracking stay with the operator (see 5b); the scout did not read the daemon's wiki config, so this holds as a lean only.
# Git-tracked, projection-only, or CRDT-only? SETTLED by 5b: split by tier (working untracked; episodic thin tracked; semantic/procedural in bags/). Survives both rounds because the alternative (all tracked) collides with the tree-clean witness and the alternative (all untracked) loses episodes on refound.
# Does the sensorium deferral cover this? R1: no embeddings, no sidecar, so no. R2: the operator's words ("neuroscience + Ai developments" memory-stage) name the same goal as the deferred arc's compaction gap. SURVIVES as the one real question: the operator ruled the deferral on 2026-10-27 naming the compaction gap; this ask on 2026-10-31 may lift it for the wiki-native, embedding-free layer. LEAN: treat this ask as the operator lifting the deferral for the plain-tiddler stage only (no vector index, no sidecar), keep the sensorium re-stand deferred. This is the only item the operator must rule; the scout will not decide it.

<<~/ahu>>

